WHAT THIS LICENCE DOES NOT COVER, and cannot:

  - The typefaces in fonts/. Each keeps its own SIL Open Font License and its
    own designer's copyright. See liner-notes.html and fonts/_sources.json.
  - The songs reachable from Pink Pony Club. Every one belongs to the artist who
    made it. None are hosted here; the jukebox links out and nothing more.
  - The borrowed names — Danny the Street, Pee-Wee's Playhouse, Pink Pony Club,
    Enid Sinclair. Homage is not licence. See liner-notes.html.
  - Recordings in audio/ made by anybody other than us — a passage read aloud,
    a yell, anything with somebody's voice in it. The words may be ours; the
    voice is not, and it carries no onward licence. ("read by" was the wording
    here until the yell button needed recordings too, and a yell is not a
    reading.) Same reasoning as the photographs below: CC BY-SA cannot be
    revoked, and a person who lends us their voice has to be able to take it
    back. Ours, recorded by us, are covered by the licence above like any other
    thing we made.
  - The community photographs on Enid's polaroid wall. Every one stays the
    property of the people in it and the person who took it, used here with
    their permission and under no onward licence at all. This exclusion is
    load-bearing rather than tidy: CC BY-SA is irrevocable and permits
    commercial reuse, so a photograph published under it could not be taken
    back even after somebody withdrew consent. We promise a photo comes down
    when its subject says so, once, without a conversation. That promise is
    only true if the licence never applied to it. See polaroids.html.

Relicensing something that is not ours would be exactly the failure this site
spends a whole page guarding against.
